 ## Scope Rule
@@ -43,7 +43,8 @@
 - A locked object must show a lock reason ("Requires: ..."), never silence.
 - Completing a step must give feedback (text + sound + visual) and move the waypoint to the next target. The new target state must be published before the marker updates.
 - Facts before comparison: the player must obtain the data (read/inspect) before a choice panel appears, and the panel must show that data next to the choices.
-- Never put answer values in tracker, hint, or panel text. Hints name the source, not the answer.
+- Tracker and hints must not state correct answer values or conclusions. They name the source and action, without revealing or identifying the correct choice.
+- Evidence shown in a comparison panel must come only from data already collected by the squad and appear next to the choices. Do not reveal uncollected evidence or label, highlight, or auto-select any choice as correct.
 - Tracker shows every parallel branch, marks the active one, and has a key to switch.
 - The waypoint targets the interactable body the player must press, shows name + distance, appears at any range, and has a straight-line fallback when no NavMesh route exists.
 - Hold actions show a progress ring and the bound key; releasing early cancels visibly.
